","text":"Whether the graph has a bridge. Stops at the first one found."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/hasbridges","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/kEdgeConnectedSubgraphs(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kEdgeConnectedSubgraphs(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kedgeconnectedsubgraphs(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-edge-connected subgraphs: the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"k-edge-connected (every pair joined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":" edge-disjoint paths inside it), ordered as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"connectedComponents()"},{"type":"text","text":". They partition the vertices, a vertex in none being a set alone."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Parallel edges are separate paths and self-loops count for nothing. Each set is refined"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kEdgeConnectedComponents(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" of its own induced subgraph until it is one class; at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most n refinements, each O(k n (n + m)). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k = 1"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the connected components in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m)."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"kEdgeConnectedSubgraphs(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kEdgeConnectedSubgraphs"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV","text":"Components"},{"ki